MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 351736019}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cd81c9ca13c84f1cb228c6051df76ab4, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Nocturne.UI::Nocturne.UI.ControlsScreen
  showOnStart: 1
  openKey: 17
  playerInput: {fileID: 1229188410}
  controls:
  - action: Move
    keyboard: WASD/Arrows
    controller: Left Stick/D-pad
  - action: Jump
    keyboard: Space
    controller: A
  - action: Interact
    keyboard: E
    controller: B
  - action: Throw
    keyboard: Q
    controller: Y
  - action: Dash
    keyboard: Shift
    controller: X
  - action: Inspect
    keyboard: R
    controller: 
  - action: Book
    keyboard: Tab
    controller: 
  - action: Shop
    keyboard: B
    controller: Select
  howToPlay: 'Start by talking to your customer to hear what they need.


    Ingredients are scattered across the shelves of your apothecary, so climb the ladders and pick up what you can find. Inspect anything new to learn its tags, then check your book whenever you forget.


    Most ingredients have a primary tag and a secondary tag, so you''ll often need to refine them first. Chopping an ingredient on the cutting board cuts out its primary tag, and the mortar packs three ingredients together into one that keeps all of their tags.


    When you''re ready, drop two ingredients into the cauldron and stir to brew. Hand the potion to your customer, who wants a primary and secondary tag.


    Inspecting, refining, brewing and asking questions all use energy. Running short on something? The shop sells quality ingredients that only carry their primary tag.'
